//! Golden test for `pr_core::file_actions::service`: every case of `tests/golden/file-action-scenarios.json` (111 cases:
//! 56 single, 55 group), generated by the C# oracle `tools/oracle-cs/Commands/W3-04.cs` (`W304Disk` / `W304Bin`) at
//! baseline d92d6aae (contract W3-04, "Golden package").
//!
//! The harness is a line-by-line port of the oracle's in-memory disk ([`ScenarioFs`] = `W304Disk`) and bin
//! ([`ScenarioBin`] = `W304Bin`), including every message text, and compares, per case: the result fields, the journal
//! lines after GUID normalization (`<id1>`, `<id2>`, ... in order of first appearance over the journal lines, then
//! `group_id`, then `entry.id` / `entry.group_id`), `journal_ends_with_crlf`, `files_after`, `dirs_after`, `recycled`,
//! `permanently_deleted_paths`, `fits_calls`, the `trace`, `busy_after` and `token_cancelled`.
//!
//! Differences that are not behaviour: the Rust journal lives at `AppPaths::journal_file` (not `C:\data\operations.jsonl`),
//! so the trace filter skips that file and its folder (the oracle skips its own journal file and `C:\data`); `Exists` is an
//! `io::Error` of kind `AlreadyExists` with the oracle's text (an `io::Error` cannot carry both a text and a raw OS code;
//! nothing in the service reads the code).

mod common_file_actions;

